Subject: [PATCH wireless v3] wifi: mt76: mt7996: replace direct WTBL access
 with MCU for station statistics
Date: Tue,  7 Apr 2026 06:45:55 -0400

Direct MMIO access to WTBL entries for airtime and RSSI statistics in
mt7996_mac_sta_poll() races with firmware, causing warnings at
mt7996_mac_wtbl_lmac_addr, MCU message timeouts, and firmware
communication breakdown. The function was called from
mt7996_mac_tx_free() on every TX-Free-Done event, compounding the
issue with heavy CPU overhead.

Replace the direct WTBL polling with firmware MCU queries:
- Airtime: UNI_ALL_STA_TXRX_AIR_TIME via the existing all_sta_info
  MCU command, with a new handler in mt7996_mcu_rx_all_sta_info_event()
- RSSI: UNI_PER_STA_RSSI via new mt7996_mcu_get_per_sta_info() using
  MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(PER_STA_INFO)

Both queries run from mt7996_mac_work() every 5th tick under dev mutex,
matching the pattern already used for TX rate, admission stats, and
MSDU count reporting.

Remove mt7996_mac_sta_poll() and its airtime_ac tracking array entirely,
along with the now-orphaned mt76_wcid_add_poll() producers in the RX
status, TX free, and TX status paths that fed the removed consumer.

The per-sta-info response handler validates the firmware response before
walking its entries, and uses bounds-checked mt76_wcid_ptr() for WLAN ID
lookup. RSSI polling is batched in groups of PER_STA_INFO_MAX_NUM to
cover the full WTBL capacity.

Vendor driver analysis (mt_wifi.ko from Xiaomi AX3000T MT7981 firmware)
confirms the RCPI-to-RSSI conversion formula (rcpi - 220) / 2 and that
the vendor never performs direct WTBL reads for statistics.

Fixes: 98686cd21624 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: add driver for MediaTek Wi-Fi 7 (802.11be) devices")
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/21177
Message-ID: <20260407104555.4342-1-joshuaklinesmith@gmail.com>
Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-wireless/patch/20260407104555.4342-1-joshuaklinesmith@gmail.com/
Signed-off-by: Joshua Klinesmith <joshuaklinesmith@gmail.com>

Project adaptation for mt76 0936617dc529ff9da0385221d3fa6de732231177:
- Add AIR_TIME to both element-size dispatch and event consumption.
- Validate ALL_STA RXD/fixed/TLV lengths, counts, duplicate/bounded WLAN IDs
  before applying a fragment; hold RCU while dereferencing station state.
- Correct donor PER_STA's copied ALL_STA header: the vendor RSSI ABI has
  4 reserved bytes plus tag/len (8 bytes), no more/sta_num fields. Derive
  count from validated TLV length and reject partial elements, excessive,
  duplicate, unsolicited or out-of-range IDs before touching RSSI/EWMA.
- Match vendor airtime's interval microseconds contract: map LMAC AC to
  mac80211 TID, register each delta once, no WTBL-style second subtraction
  or unit scaling. Poll whole-device statistics only on the first running
  PHY; leave per-PHY MIB updates and WED guards intact.
- Discard reserved/unavailable RCPI chains; preserve previous signal and
  EWMA on malformed responses, missing links/PHYs or invalid signal. MCU
  send errors return immediately; malformed-response skbs are freed. The
  next work period retries polling;
  no direct-WTBL fallback is reintroduced. Full batches already consumed
  before a later RSSI batch error are not rolled back.

ABI/semantics reference: MediaTek's 0065 patch at feeds commit
00a8c1e85ec32003d9260ea34bc9ecbc15e8d4a8 (Benjamin Lin / Yi-Chia Hsieh):
https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/00a8c1e85ec32003d9260ea34bc9ecbc15e8d4a8/autobuild/autobuild_5.4_mac80211_release/mt7988_wifi7_mac80211_mlo/package/kernel/mt76/patches/0065-mtk-mt76-mt7996-get-airtime-and-RSSI-via-MCU-command.patch

No token-reclamation (0006) behavior is included. This source adaptation
has isolated patch/source-contract tests, not compilation or W1700K
firmware/hardware validation. Actual firmware ABI, counter reset/units,
RSSI freshness and multi-radio/MLO behavior still require device testing.

